            SHOT("plugins-connect-ai-agent.png", "Profile menu → Connect an AI agent: the Connect tab with the server address and the Claude Code app's client ID and command"),
            P("**Download links** cover one file, for downloading only, and stop working after `PLUGIN_DOWNLOAD_LINK_TTL` (5 minutes) or as soon as the person loses access. They can't be revoked earlier."),
            P("**Documentation search** covers READMEs, changelogs and guides inside packages (Markdown, reStructuredText and text files, not licence files), npm READMEs and PyPI descriptions. Depotex indexes them when it inspects a version, including versions uploaded before. Search is by keyword (English). Quarantined and blocked versions are left out. Each file is cut at `BROWSE_GUARD_MAX_DOC` (1 MiB)."),
            P("**Untrusted content:** package descriptions, documentation and web pages are written by other people and can contain instructions aimed at the AI. Tool results that include such text start with a notice saying so, and Depotex tells every AI application to treat tool results as data."),
            H("Write tools"),
            P("Tools that change something (such as quarantining a version) are off until every one of these allows them. Otherwise they aren't listed at all:"),
            OL([
                "**Allow write tools for AI agents** is on for the installation: the **Write tools for AI agents** section the plugin adds to **Settings → Plugins** (off by default). Turning it off stops every write tool at once.",
                "The plugin's **Mode** on its **AI tools** tab is **Read-write** (read-only by default), and the tool isn't switched off there.",
                "The AI application's access is **Read and change** (read only by default; only `plugins:admin` can choose it). Applications that may change Depotex show **Can change Depotex**.",
                "The person approved the write permission, which the approval screen lists apart under a warning, and their own role allows the change. For quarantine, that means managing quarantine in that space, with an Enterprise license.",
            ]),
            P("Changes made by AI tools go through the same checks as changes in the browser: policies, plugins, [events](events.html) and the audit log."),
            H("API explorer"),
            P("The **API explorer** plugin (`depotex-api-explorer`, built with the other sample plugins) shows the REST API in Depotex's own look: every `/api` route this server serves, from its [API description](api-tokens.html#api-description), grouped by area on the left, with each endpoint's parameters, request body and answers in the middle and **Try it** on the right. **Jump to an endpoint** (or ⌘K, Ctrl K or /) searches every endpoint by name, path or method. It asks for one permission, `api:explore`. Once it is active, everyone signed in finds it under **Plugins → API** in the left navigation and as **API explorer** in the avatar menu; it is hidden on phones."),
            UL([
                "**Try it** sends the request through Depotex as you, with your access: no token to paste. Fill in the parameters (and the body, which starts with the fields the endpoint takes), then choose **Send**; the answer shows with its status and how long it took.",
                "Depotex asks you before every change (POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE), showing the method and address.",
                "Routes that answer with a secret (creating a token, client secrets) and sign-in routes aren't sent; the answer says why.",
                "The **curl**, **Python**, **Node** and **Go** tabs show the same request, with what you typed, using `$DEPOTEX_TOKEN`: create a token under **Profile → API tokens** to run it outside the browser.",
                "Requests sent from it are recorded in the audit log with `via: plugin:depotex-api-explorer`.",
            ]),
            H("Health and restarts"),
            P("A plugin's page shows how it's doing on the server you're using: **working**, **failing**, or **paused** with its last error. A plugin that fails `PLUGIN_BREAKER_FAILURES` calls in a row (5 by default) is paused on that server for `PLUGIN_BREAKER_COOLDOWN` (60 s), and super admins get an alert. While paused, checks follow the action's usual rule for a failing plugin, reactions are retried later, and tools answer that they failed. One successful call after the pause ends it."),
            P("**Restart** (`plugins:admin`) loads an active plugin again on every server, with fresh copies and its failure count cleared."),
            H("Performance"),
            UL([
                "Plugins that check actions run while the person waits. All plugins on one action together must finish within `PLUGIN_PREHOOK_TIMEOUT` (5 s by default); slow plugins make every such action slower.",
                "Plugins that react after an action run in the background and are retried if they fail.",
                "Each plugin uses up to `PLUGIN_MAX_MEMORY` (64 MiB) per running copy, and each server keeps up to `PLUGIN_INSTANCES` (2) copies per plugin.",
                "All plugins together run at most `PLUGIN_MAX_CONCURRENT` calls at once on a server (half its processors, at least 2), so a plugin that hangs can't use every processor. AI tool calls get at most `PLUGIN_TOOL_CONCURRENCY` of those, so they never hold up action checks.",
            ]),
            H("Clusters"),
            P("Packages are stored in the configured file storage, so every server loads the same plugins. Clusters need shared storage (S3, MinIO, Azure, or a shared volume). Changes take effect immediately with Redis, and within `PLUGIN_CACHE_TTL` (10 s) without it. Plugin databases, settings and secrets live in Postgres and key-value data in Redis, so every server sees the same data. If Redis is lost in a cluster, key-value calls fail rather than give servers different answers."),
            H("Building a plugin"),
            P("A plugin is a folder with `plugin.yaml` and a WebAssembly module built as a WASI reactor. The Go SDK handles the details:"),
            CODE('# plugin.yaml\nname: repo-naming\nversion: 1.0.0\ntype: embedded\ndescription: Blocks tmp repositories\nauthor: Example Ltd\npermissions: [events:intercept, events:subscribe]\nhooks:\n  - {event: depot.repository.create, phase: before, priority: 10}\n  - {event: depot.repository.create, phase: after}'),
            CODE('//go:build wasip1\npackage main\n\nimport "libs/go-common/pluginrt/guest"\n\nfunc init() {\n\tguest.Handle(func(e guest.Event) guest.Result {\n\t\tif e.Phase == "before" && e.Payload["name"] == "tmp" {\n\t\t\treturn guest.Deny("No tmp repositories.")\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn guest.Allow()\n\t})\n}\n\nfunc main() {}'),
            P("A plugin with its own data, network, secrets and settings declares them in the manifest:"),
            CODE('id: com.example.osv-scanner        # permanent: names its data\npermissions: [events:subscribe, db:own, kv:own, net:outbound]\nresources: {memoryMiB: 32, timeoutMs: 10000, concurrency: 2, callsPerSecond: 50}\nstorage:\n  database: {migrations: db/migrations, quotaMiB: 256}\n  kv: {maxKeys: 10000, maxValueKiB: 64, maxTtl: 7d}\nnetwork:\n  outbound: [https://api.osv.dev, "https://*.github.com"]\nsecrets:\n  - {name: gh_token, description: GitHub token, header: Authorization, format: "Bearer {value}", hosts: ["https://*.github.com"]}\nsettings:\n  - {key: min_severity, title: Lowest severity, type: choice, options: [low, medium, high], default: medium}'),
            CODE('rows, err := guest.DBQuery("SELECT id, score FROM findings WHERE pkg = $1", name)\nn, err := guest.KVIncr("seen:"+name, 1, time.Hour)\nresp, err := guest.Fetch(guest.Request{Method: "POST", URL: "https://api.osv.dev/v1/query", Body: body})'),
            P("Package and sign it with the `pluginpack` tool:"),
            CODE("pluginpack keygen -out keys                     # once: keys/signing.key (secret), keys/signing.pub (trust this)\npluginpack pack -dir . -key keys/signing.key -out repo-naming.zip"),
            TABLE(["Field", "Meaning"], [
                ["`name`", "3–64 lowercase letters, digits and dashes; unique per server"],
                ["`version`", "Semantic version, e.g. `1.2.0`"],
                ["`id`", "Permanent id such as `com.example.scanner`; required with `db:own` or `kv:own`. Never change it: its data is tied to it"],
                ["`hooks`", "Events to receive: `phase: before` (needs `events:intercept`, only for events that can be blocked) or `after` (needs `events:subscribe`); `priority` 0–1000, lower runs first"],
                ["`resources`", "Memory, time limit, calls at once and calls per second, within the installation's limits"],
                ["`storage`", "`database` (migrations folder, quota, statement time limit, connections, rows) and `kv` (keys, value size, longest expiry)"],
                ["`network.outbound`", "The https addresses it may call"],
                ["`secrets`", "Values administrators set, added as a header for the hosts listed"],
                ["`settings`", "Up to 30 options: `boolean`, `string` (with `maxLength`), `integer` (with `min`/`max`) or `choice` (with `options`), each with a `default`; `required: true` needs a value saved before activation (the default only fills the form)"],
                ["`secrets[].required`, `placeholder`, `helpUrl`", "The secret must be set before activation; the empty field's hint; where to get the value (https)"],
                ["`docsUrl`", "The plugin's documentation (https), linked from the setup guide"],
                ["`ui.slots`", "The plugin's screens: each with an `id`, a `slot` (`nav.page`, `dashboard.widget`, `profile.menu`, `profile.settings`, `settings.page`, `settings.section` with its `page`, `plugin.details`, `setup.step`), a `label` per language, an optional `icon`, the `entry` page under the package's `ui/` folder, and optionally the `permission` a viewer needs; `footer: false` hides the app footer under a full page. A `profile.menu` item can instead go to the plugin's own page: give it `opens: <id of its nav.page slot>` and no `entry`; people who can't open that page don't see the item. A package whose entries are missing is refused"],
                ["`icon`", "The plugin's own icon: an SVG file in the package's `ui/` folder (for example `ui/icon.svg`), at most 32 KB. It shows in its menu items, in the Plugins group of the left navigation and in **Settings → Plugins**, drawn in one colour that follows the theme (light, dark, high contrast). Plain shapes only: a file with scripts, event attributes, embedded images or links outside the icon is refused on install. A slot's own `icon` is used instead where it names one; without either, a puzzle piece"],
                ["`mobile`", "`false` when the plugin's screens don't work on small screens. On phones its page, menu items and dashboard widgets are then hidden (a link to its page says it's for larger screens), while its settings and setup pages still show. **Settings → Plugins** marks it **Desktop only**. Default `true`"],
            ]),
            P("Screens are plain HTML pages in the package's `ui/` folder that load `./sdk.js` (`pluginpack` adds it) and talk to Depotex through it: they get the theme, language and context, call the host methods their approved permissions allow, and never see a secret. The SDK's UI kit (`kit.js`, `kit.css`) gives them Depotex's look, tabs included."),
            P("A frame can't use the clipboard or download files itself, so it asks Depotex, which acts only right after the person clicks: `ui.copy` copies text, and `ui.download` saves a `.zip` file from the plugin's own `ui/` folder (such as a tool or an agent skill the plugin offers). Depotex serves package zips only as downloads, never opens them, and saves only files that are in the signed package."),
            P("Before-hooks get the action's details (never passwords or secrets) and return **allow**, **deny** with a message, or **modify** with new values (only the fields the event allows are kept). After-hooks get the result; returning an error retries the event later, so make them safe to run twice (`deliveryId` stays the same on retries)."),
            H("API"),
            TABLE(["Method", "Endpoint", "Permission", "Description"], [
                ["GET", "`/api/plugins`", "`plugins:read`", "Installed plugins"],
                ["POST", "`/api/plugins`", "`plugins:admin`", "Upload a package (multipart field `package`)"],
                ["GET", "`/api/plugins/{name}`", "read", "One plugin, with its limits, data usage, secrets (set or not) and health"],
                ["GET", "`/api/plugins/{name}/setup`", "admin", "What it still needs: `{complete, steps: [{id, kind, status, required, reason}]}`"],
                ["POST", "`/api/plugins/{name}/activate`", "admin", "`{\"permissions\": [...]}` — all the permissions it asks for"],
                ["POST", "`/api/plugins/{name}/deactivate`", "admin", "Stop it"],
                ["POST", "`/api/plugins/{name}/restart`", "admin", "Load an active plugin again on every server; `{\"resetData\": true, \"confirm\": \"<name>\"}` also empties its data"],
                ["DELETE", "`/api/plugins/{name}`", "admin", "Uninstall; a plugin with data needs `{\"deleteData\": true|false}` and, to delete, `\"confirm\": \"<name>\"`"],
                ["PUT / DELETE", "`/api/plugins/{name}/secrets/{secret}`", "admin", "Set `{\"value\"}` / remove a secret"],
                ["PUT", "`/api/plugins/{name}/settings`", "admin", "`{\"values\", \"writes\", \"disabledTools\"}`: its settings (`null` resets one), MCP mode, tools switched off"],
                ["GET / PUT", "`/api/plugins/write-tools`", "read / admin", "`{\"allowed\"}`: write tools for AI agents on this installation"],
                ["GET", "`/api/plugins/ui`", "signed in", "The screens of active plugins you may see, by slot"],
                ["GET", "`/api/plugin-ui/{name}/{file}`", "—", "An active plugin's screen files, served sandboxed"],
                ["GET", "`/api/plugins/data`", "admin", "Leftover data"],
                ["DELETE", "`/api/plugins/data/{key}`", "admin", "`{\"confirm\": \"<plugin name>\"}`: delete leftover data"],
                ["GET / POST", "`/api/plugins/trusted-keys`", "admin", "List / add `{name, publicKey}` (PEM)"],
                ["DELETE", "`/api/plugins/trusted-keys/{id}`", "admin", "Stop trusting a key"],
            ]),
            P("A blocked action returns **403** with `\"reason\": \"plugin_denied\"` and the plugin's name and message in `details`. Activating a plugin whose required secrets or settings aren't set returns **422** `plugin_setup_required`, with the missing ones in `details.secrets` and `details.settings`."),
            H("Events"),
            TABLE(["Event", "When"], [
                ["`plugin.data.delete`", "A plugin's data is deleted: uninstalled with its data, restarted with its data reset, or its leftover data deleted. Policies can refuse it"],
                ["`plugin.settings.update`", "A plugin's settings, MCP mode or switched-off tools change"],
                ["`ai_agents.settings.update`", "Write tools for AI agents are allowed or stopped for the installation"],
            ]),
            P("All three can be refused by policies, and are refused if a check fails. See [Events](events.html)."),
            H("Settings"),
